{
  "_id": "1bdsbFD4C4rgueBX",
  "name": "Soulbound Arsenal",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/weapons/swords/sword-guard-purple.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<blockquote><p><em>The weapon is not carried so much as recalled. It answers to a shape you hold in mind rather than a shape it was forged into, it cannot be taken from you by any means, and on the days you are too broken to lift it, it has been known to fight on without you.</em></p></blockquote>\n<p><strong>1st Level</strong></p><ul><li>Gain a bonded weapon. As a free action once per round it takes the form of any simple, martial, or advanced melee or ranged weapon.<ul><li>Ranged forms generate their own ammunition and never need reloading.</li></ul></li><li>It cannot be disarmed, stolen, or left behind, and returns to your hand at the start of your turn.</li><li>It is a +1 striking weapon.</li><li>Your proficiency rank with it equals your highest weapon or unarmed proficiency rank, regardless of its current form.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>3rd Level</strong></p><ul><li>Whenever you change its form, choose one precious material. It counts as that material for overcoming resistances, weaknesses, and immunities.<ul><li>It gains none of that material's other properties, and its grade is the highest available at your level.</li></ul></li><li>The weapon gains its own reaction each round, separate from yours, usable only for Bonded Strike.<ul><li><strong>Bonded Strike</strong> [reaction] <strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy moves within the weapon's reach. <strong>Effect</strong> The weapon Strikes that enemy. This Strike neither counts toward nor against your multiple attack penalty.</li></ul></li></ul>\n<p><strong>5th Level</strong></p><ul><li>+1 striking with one property rune.</li><li>Choose a weapon group. You gain its critical specialization effect with this weapon in any form, and may change the group whenever you change its form.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>7th Level</strong></p><ul><li>+2 striking, two property runes.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>9th Level</strong></p><ul><li>+2 greater striking, two property runes.</li><li>The weapon acts independently using your statistics, and may use Bonded Strike even while you are Grabbed, Restrained, Immobilized, or unconscious.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>11th Level</strong></p><ul><li>You may change the weapon's form twice per round.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>13th Level</strong></p><ul><li>+3 greater striking, three property runes.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>15th Level</strong></p><ul><li>+3 major striking. Gains the deadly d12 trait.</li><li>The weapon gains a second reaction each round, usable only for Bonded Strike.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>17th Level</strong></p><ul><li>+4 major striking, four property runes.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>19th Level</strong></p><ul><li>You may change the weapon's form any number of times per round.</li></ul>\n<p><em>Property runes are determined whenever you change the weapon's form and must be of a level equal to or less than your level + 2.</em></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>In Foundry:</strong> put any weapon in your inventory and add the <em>Soulbound Arsenal</em> tag under Other Tags on its Details tab. It then uses your highest weapon proficiency, carries the potency and striking runes for your level, counts as the precious material set in your effects panel (from 3rd), has the critical specialization of the group set there (from 5th), and gains deadly d12 at 15th. Use <strong>Reshape Bonded Weapon</strong> from your Actions tab to change its form; the dialog carries your property runes across and warns about any that would not work on the new form. Bonded Strike is on your Actions tab from 3rd.</p>\n<p>For the table: the weapon's own reactions (one from 3rd, two from 15th), never being disarmed and returning to your hand, acting while you cannot from 9th, and the number of form changes per round. The property rune count (one at 5th, two at 7th, three at 13th, four at 17th) and their level cap are yours to keep; the reshape dialog states both.</p>",
      "gm": ""
    },
